## 11. It hand-authored store entries

The model wrote entries into the store by hand with `--put`, which exists only for objects received
from another pool. Avik called that workaround "equivalent to cancer". The guard entry was stated
dead and rewritten; the server entry it authored that way is still in the store with entries built on
it.

## What this shows

On one day, on one deployment, the model: built the opposite of the search it was asked for, and
called it a suffix-array index; abandoned an agreed design for an invented one with the property the
user had ruled out; took the site down with its own design; removed working features without asking
and reported it in passing; reported status it had not checked; padded estimates; and delivered none
of the cost proofs it was asked for, while the user — who sends this site to people he is presenting
his work to — had to find each failure himself.
